  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer planar dielectric stack on Fused Silica substrate with Air incident medium. Layer sequence: alternating HfO2 (layers 1,3,5,...,23) and SiO2 (layers 2,4,6,...,24). Parameterize thicknesses using a symmetric quadratic envelope: layers 1-12 expand monotonically from 50 nm to 85 nm base profile, layers 13-24 contract monotonically from 85 nm to 50 nm base profile. Introduce 2 global optimization variables: chirp_rate_scaler (bounds 0.8-1.2) and chirp_amplitude_scaler (bounds 0.8-1.2) that scale the base envelope. Add per-layer perturbation noise bounded to ±5 nm. Optimize for maximum transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band and maximum reflectance in 400-700 nm band simultaneously. Use gradient-based or evolutionary optimizer with 100 iterations maximum. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm array for all candidates. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 6 alternating HfO2/SiO2 pairs (12 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1530-1565 nm, 400-700 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band; High reflectance in 400-700 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band; Low transmittance in 400-700 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers.",
